 9710 21268  9710 10 codex -m gpt-6.1-sol -c model_reasoning_effort=max -c mcp_servers.graft.enabled=false -s workspace-write -a never -C /Volumes/memit/llm-database-poc-mirror/arhugula-persistent-memory/.claude/worktrees/c10k-route-a MB33, from MAESTRO27. You build the NEW-1 launch recorder, test-first, fixture-only. The operator authorized exactly ONE real run of the NEW-1 supervisor. The reviewer (Astra) set launch conditions C1 and C3 that the supervisor itself cannot satisfy; your recorder satisfies them from outside. You never run the real supervisor or the real worker.\012\012Read first: results/mathlab_staging/new1_launch_readiness_astra.md items 2 (C1), 5 (C3), 6 (C2), 7 (abort accounting) and 9 (the endorsed command). Then cat -n tools/new1_supervisor.py lines 160-200 (retry scanner), 290-360 (signal guard, worker reap), 425-560 (supervise: admission, worker spawn) and 600-651 (halt path, main). Cite file:line for every claim you make about supervisor behaviour.\012\012<context>\012Facts already established (verify them, do not re-derive at length):\012- main() (tools/new1_supervisor.py:632-651) creates results/mathlab_staging/runs/new1_<UTC> with exist_ok=False, runs admission INSIDE the run, then spawns the worker as `nice -n 10 <python> -B tools/new1_geometry.py ...` with start_new_session=True (:532), so the worker leads its own process group and its niceness is the supervisor's niceness + 10. It prints the outcome code to stdout and exits 0 on PASS, 3 otherwise.\012- Admission inside the run calls tools/c10w_p2_gate.py check_gpu (:73-84). blocking_processes (:43-54) excludes only the admission process's own PID: any other process whose executable basename matches (?i)^python[0-9.]* and is not in EXEMPT blocks admission. A refusal there is INVALID-ADMISSION and consumes the one authorization.\012- The retry scanner (:170-191) counts only `halted` events with reason STOPPED-RESOURCE/STOPPED-DEADLINE. A deadline can end the run with no `halted` event (verdict item 5), so that scanner undercounts.\012</context>\012\012<requirements>\0121. tools/new1_dispatch.sh, a /bin/zsh script (no Python process may be alive while the supervisor runs; see the negative example). Run as `cd <worktree> && tools/new1_dispatch.sh <hashes.sha256> <expected-HEAD> <authorization-file>`. Every repo path derives from the cwd (ROOT), so tests can run it inside a fixture tree.\0122. Pre-invocation checks, in this order; the first failure writes refused_before_invocation.json (check name, command, output, exit) and exits nonzero WITHOUT invoking anything. Authorization is not consumed by a pre-invocation refusal.\012   a. create results/mathlab_staging/new1_dispatch_<UTC>/ exclusively (mkdir without -p; refuse if it exists);\012   b. refuse if any earlier results/mathlab_staging/new1_dispatch_*/invocation.json names the same authorization file SHA-256 (single use, code-enforced);\012   c. `git rev-parse HEAD` equals <expected-HEAD>, and `git status --porcelain` is empty for every path in <hashes.sha256>;\012   d. `/usr/bin/shasum -a 256 -c <hashes.sha256>` passes (file is in shasum format; C4 will produce the real one with the 8 pinned files);\012   e. the recorder's own niceness is 0 (`/bin/ps -o nice= -p $$`), so the supervisor starts at 0 and the worker lands at 10;\012   f. free space on ROOT's volume >= 21 GiB (/bin/df -k);\012   g. `LLMDB_ROOT=$ROOT /usr/bin/python3 tools/engine_fingerprint.py` exits 0;\012   h. the read-only admission dry probe exits 0 and prints allowed True: `LLMDB_ROOT=$ROOT $ROOT/.venv/bin/python -B -c 'import sys;sys.path.insert(0,".");from tools import mathlab_admit as A;d=A.probe("cpu");print(d["allowed"],d["reasons"],d["checks"]["gpu"].get("blocking_processes"));sys.exit(0 if d["allowed"] else 1)'`;\012   i. re-run check d immediately before invocation.\012   Save each check's command, stdout, stderr and exit in the dispatch dir. A test may only make a check stricter (e.g. raise the free-space floor through an env var); nothing may loosen or skip one.\0123. Invocation. Write invocation.json (UTC, authorization file path + SHA-256, the exact argv/env) BEFORE starting; its existence means the authorization is consumed. Then run the endorsed command from verdict item 9 verbatim (same env assignments, `$PWD/.venv/bin/python -B $PWD/tools/new1_supervisor.py --prereg-sha 1616c860c38b65acbabb7ec472a1233b30291337e86a7739271df0c4bd1c9d0f`), in the background, stdout/stderr to supervisor_stdout.log / supervisor_stderr.log in the dispatch dir (not in the runs/ namespace). Record the supervisor PID and its niceness.\0124. Worker observation (C1). Poll `/bin/ps -axo pid=,ppid=,pgid=,nice=,command=` until a process appears whose ppid is the supervisor, whose executable basename is a python (after `nice` has exec'd; the transient `nice -n 10 ...` process itself does not count) and whose command contains tools/new1_geometry.py, or until the supervisor exits. Record pid, ppid, pgid, nice, command and the observation time in worker.json. If the worker is observed with nice != 10, or ps fails while the supervisor is alive: send SIGINT to the supervisor PID only (cite the source lines showing SIGINT routes to the reaping halt path), record stop_reason, and wait for it to exit. No escalation beyond SIGINT; a supervisor that does not exit within 60 s is recorded as such for the operator. If the supervisor exits before any worker appears, record worker: none observed.\0125. Exit capture (C3). Record the supervisor exit status, end time, and the namespace: exactly one new results/mathlab_staging/runs/new1_* directory that was absent from a snapshot taken before invocation (zero or several is recorded as an anomaly, not guessed). Post-exit disposition: list every live process whose pid is the worker pid or whose pgid is the worker pgid; nonempty means disposition UNREAPED and the receipt says subsequent compute is blocked until resolved.\0126. tools/new1_dispatch_report.py, stdlib only, run by the recorder AFTER the supervisor has exited (Python is safe then). It writes dispatch_receipt.json:\012   - outcome: stdout outcome code, terminal event found in events.jsonl or not (derive the terminal event types from tools/mathlab_events.py and the supervisor; cite lines), exit status;\012   - verdict_status COMPLETE only when the terminal event, the stdout code and the exit status agree; otherwise INCOMPLETE with "no prediction verdict";\012   - abort accounting: this dispatch counts as a resource/deadline abort when a halted event, the stdout code, or supervisor stderr names STOPPED-RESOURCE or STOPPED-DEADLINE; prior_aborts uses the scanner's rule (:185-190) over the other new1_* namespaces plus earlier dispatch receipts; report total and third_abort_rule_reached (total >= 3);\012   - authorization_consumed: true whenever invocation.json exists, including admission refusal.\0127. Tests first, in tests/test_new1_dispatch.py, each against a fixture ROOT tree (fake .venv/bin/python as a symlink to a real Python, fake tools/new1_supervisor.py, tools/new1_geometry.py, engine_fingerprint.py and mathlab_admit.py; a throwaway git repo for HEAD). Each must be RED before the recorder exists and GREEN after:\012   T1 a fixture dispatch's recorder process line, fed to tools.c10w_p2_gate.blocking_processes, is not a blocker;\012   T2 happy path: supervisor PID, worker pid/pgid/nice=10, namespace, exit 0, disposition clean, COMPLETE;\012   T3 each pre-check failure separately (2b-2h, plus 2i via a hash change between d and i): no invocation.json, no supervisor process started;\012   T4 recorder started under `nice -n 1`: refused at 2e;\012   T5 fixture worker spawned with niceness 3: SIGINT sent to the supervisor, stop_reason recorded, authorization consumed;\012   T6 STOPPED-DEADLINE on stderr, no halted event, exit 3: counted abort, INCOMPLETE;\012   T7 STOPPED-RESOURCE with a halted event: counted abort;\012   T8 admission refusal inside the run (no worker): consumed, wor